"text": "When you touch the bug, it disappears into thin air. And if you try recording it with a regular camera, you'll only see a tiny blur where the bug was. So how does this bug disappear? It starts when a fork-shaped body part shoots out, slapping against the ground and spinning the bug in the air 30 times within a single blink of an eye. But when it falls back down, the flipping motion makes it hard to land in one area. So the bug races up a sticky tube. And when it hits the ground, the tube slaps onto the surface, helping the bug stick a perfect landing before you can even realize what's happening.",
